# SQL's `IS NULL`: DS0105 with a fix to `isnull(...)`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where amount is null
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..36
  PIPELINE@0..35
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..35
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..35
        NAME_REF@21..27
          IDENT@21..27 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
        IDENT@28..30 "is"
        WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
        NULL_KW@31..35 "null"
  WHITESPACE@35..36 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `is null` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:29
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where amount is null
  |                             ^^^^^^^ this is SQL's null test
  |
  = help: test for null with `isnull(...)`: `isnull(amount)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where isnull(amount)
which parses without errors
